  "changes": [
    "Ordinary Paint captures object-local reflected ray hits, X symmetry and f64 relative mirror offset, using shared Rust contact preparation.",
    "Primary then mirrored requests blend overlapping RGB/material values with a Float32 write between the two passes.",
    "Both actual press and dab alpha tracks use the shared exclusive frame lease; mirrored alpha X lookup uses the existing core kernel.",
    "Additive retained-source-controls entry accepts validated alpha/mirror requests over the actual immutable warm normal producer. The previous alphaNone-only API and its original rejection tests remain intact.",
    "Primary miss resets copied mirror radius to zero, preserving a finite empty selection/no-op rather than inventing a stale radius.",
    "Normal sidebar exposes X symmetry and a strict f64 relative-offset numeric editor. Existing settings and file formats remain unchanged."
  ],
